window.US_GAME_PREVIEWS={"asOf":"2026-10-15","method":"Based on official results, available player box scores and credited school reporting. Team averages are not adjusted for strength of schedule.","games":[{"id":"2026-10-15-alberta-regina","away":"alberta","home":"regina","date":"2026-10-15","conference":"CW","asOf":"2026-10-15","title":"Rams look to stop slide against Golden Bears","paragraphs":["Regina has been close. What the Rams have not done lately is win.","Losses to UBC, Saskatchewan and Calgary have come by a combined 13 points, leaving Regina at 2–3 heading into Thursday's home game against Alberta. The latest was the toughest to take on the scoreboard, a 14–13 loss to the Dinos on October 3.","The Rams have allowed 18.6 points a game, a much better mark than Alberta's 40.0. That has kept Regina competitive, but it has not been enough to get through a stretch in which each game has stayed within reach.","Alberta, meanwhile, has shown two very different sides on offence. The Golden Bears beat Calgary 42–35 on September 25, then managed just three points in an 18–3 loss to Manitoba a week later. At 1–4, they need more of the team that beat the Dinos.","Regina won the first meeting 39–8 on September 4. Alberta's offence will have to offer more resistance in the rematch, especially against a defence that has given the Rams a chance to win most weeks.","The Golden Bears are averaging 15 points a game. Regina is scoring 25.2. For Alberta, a repeat of its Calgary performance would change the complexion of this matchup. For the Rams, the immediate job is turning another winnable game into a result."],"notes":["Records and team scoring use regular-season results completed before October 15. Exhibitions are excluded.","Player totals use the available box scores and may be incomplete. The Hec Crighton Watch is CanUFootball’s own list."],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-15","label":"Official national schedule"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260904_pg8n.xml","label":"September 4 · Regina at Alberta"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260911_19fu.xml","label":"September 11 · Alberta at UBC"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260918_mge2.xml","label":"September 18 · Saskatchewan at Alberta"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260925_jbqx.xml","label":"September 25 · Alberta at Calgary"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261002_k48e.xml","label":"October 2 · Manitoba at Alberta"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260911_hvcf.xml","label":"September 11 · Manitoba at Regina"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260918_y81r.xml","label":"September 18 · Regina at UBC"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_u9sf.xml","label":"September 26 · Saskatchewan at Regina"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261003_hww9.xml","label":"October 3 · Regina at Calgary"}]},{"id":"2026-10-16-calgary-ubc","away":"calgary","home":"ubc","date":"2026-10-16","conference":"CW","asOf":"2026-10-15","title":"UBC gets another shot at Calgary after opening loss","paragraphs":["UBC has had more than a month to think about its season-opening loss to Calgary. Friday brings the chance to do something about it.","The Thunderbirds host the Dinos after losing that first meeting 23–7. Much has changed since then: UBC won three straight before a 34–24 loss to Saskatchewan, while Calgary arrives at 2–3 following a 14–13 win over Regina.","The rematch puts UBC's running game in the spotlight. Marvyn Larozar has rushed for 713 yards in the four games included in CanUFootball's player totals, earning a place on the site's Hec Crighton Watch. Keeping him involved would help the Thunderbirds avoid the kind of offensive afternoon they had in Calgary.","The Dinos have their own playmakers. UBC's pregame reporting identifies receiver Matt Sibley as a major threat, giving the Thunderbirds something else to worry about if they commit too much attention elsewhere.","Calgary has averaged 28.2 points a game, slightly more than UBC's 26.0, but the Thunderbirds have allowed fewer points. Their defence gave up just six in a win over Manitoba before surrendering 34 to Saskatchewan.","UBC is 3–2 and looking to put another win between itself and Calgary. The Dinos can pull level in wins by repeating what worked in the opener. For the Thunderbirds, the first requirement is simple: produce more than seven points this time."],"notes":["Records and team scoring use regular-season results completed before October 15. Exhibitions are excluded.","Player totals use the available box scores and may be incomplete. The Hec Crighton Watch is CanUFootball’s own list."],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-16","label":"Official national schedule"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260904_bx7n.xml","label":"September 4 · UBC at Calgary"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260911_j4p4.xml","label":"September 11 · Calgary at Saskatchewan"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_96n6.xml","label":"September 19 · Calgary at Manitoba"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260925_jbqx.xml","label":"September 25 · Alberta at Calgary"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261003_hww9.xml","label":"October 3 · Regina at Calgary"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260911_19fu.xml","label":"September 11 · Alberta at UBC"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260918_y81r.xml","label":"September 18 · Regina at UBC"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_ncut.xml","label":"September 26 · UBC at Manitoba"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261003_8tvd.xml","label":"October 3 · UBC at Saskatchewan"},{"url":"https://bearsandpandas.ca/sports/football/stats/2026/university-of-british-columbia/boxscore/8947","label":"Marvyn Larozar · player statistics"},{"url":"https://gobisons.ca/sports/football/stats/2026/ubc-thunderbirds/boxscore/9303","label":"Marvyn Larozar · player statistics"},{"url":"https://huskies.usask.ca/sports/football/stats/2026-27/ubc-thunderbirds/boxscore/6999","label":"Marvyn Larozar · player statistics"},{"url":"https://www.reginacougars.com/sports/football/stats/2026/ubc/boxscore/11425","label":"Marvyn Larozar · player statistics"},{"url":"https://gothunderbirds.ca/news/2026/10/14/football-navacord-bc-insurance-preview-t-birds-host-dinos-for-key-shot-at-redemption.aspx","label":"UBC Thunderbirds · pregame reporting"}]},{"id":"2026-10-16-concordia-montreal","away":"concordia","home":"montreal","date":"2026-10-16","conference":"RSEQ","asOf":"2026-10-15","title":"Stingers face stiff test against Carabins","paragraphs":["Concordia has been searching for points. A visit to Montréal is an uncomfortable place to continue that search.","The Stingers are 1–4 after a 48–15 loss to Laval, and they have yet to score 20 points in a regular-season game. Friday's opponent has averaged 38.8, leaving Concordia with little reason to expect that another low-scoring offensive effort will be enough.","Montréal is 4–1, though its last outing was anything but comfortable. The Carabins beat Sherbrooke 23–17 on October 3 after losing 42–34 to Laval the previous week.","That narrow win gives Concordia something to consider. Montréal can be made to work for a result, but the Stingers must be able to hold up their end when they have the ball. Their 10–5 win over Bishop's showed they can survive a defensive struggle. Their other recent results have been less forgiving.","Concordia has allowed 29.4 points a game while scoring 11.0. Those numbers put pressure on an offence that cannot afford to spend the evening handing the ball back without points.","For Montréal, the chance is to make Concordia chase the game. For the Stingers, staying within reach will require longer drives, better use of scoring chances and a defensive effort that gives their offence time to settle in."],"notes":["Records and team scoring use regular-season results completed before October 15. Exhibitions are excluded.","Player totals use the available box scores and may be incomplete. The Hec Crighton Watch is CanUFootball’s own list."],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-16","label":"Official national schedule"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-09-05","label":"September 5 · Concordia at Laval"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260912_ppda.xml","label":"September 12 · Montréal at Concordia"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_hi62.xml","label":"September 19 · McGill at Concordia"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_shbp.xml","label":"September 26 · Concordia at Bishop's"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261003_xhzw.xml","label":"October 3 · Laval at Concordia"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-09-04","label":"September 4 · Montréal at Sherbrooke"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260918_lxef.xml","label":"September 18 · Bishop's at Montréal"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_3enl.xml","label":"September 26 · Montréal at Laval"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-03","label":"October 3 · Sherbrooke at Montréal"}]},{"id":"2026-10-16-manitoba-saskatchewan","away":"manitoba","home":"saskatchewan","date":"2026-10-16","conference":"CW","asOf":"2026-10-15","title":"Huskies seek payback against Bisons in Saskatoon","paragraphs":["Saskatchewan has beaten everyone it has faced since losing to Manitoba in the season opener. Now the Huskies get the Bisons again.","Friday's rematch in Saskatoon gives Saskatchewan a chance to answer that 40–22 loss and clinch a playoff berth, according to the Huskies' game notes. Four straight wins have taken them to 4–1 and changed the outlook considerably since that opening defeat.","The offence has been a big reason. Saskatchewan scored 65 points against Alberta, 38 against Regina and 34 against UBC in its last three games. Quarterback Anton Amundrud has thrown for 1,543 yards in the five games included in CanUFootball's totals and is on the site's Hec Crighton Watch.","Manitoba has already shown it can beat this team. The Bisons also come back from the conference bye with a good defensive result behind them, having held Alberta to three points in an 18–3 win on October 2.","That followed a much different afternoon against UBC, which beat Manitoba 31–6. The Bisons are 3–2, averaging 22 points and allowing 23 a game.","Saskatchewan's scoring average is up to 40.6. Manitoba does not have to erase that entire threat to win, as the opener showed, but it needs enough stops to keep its own offence from having to trade touchdowns all night."],"notes":["Records and team scoring use regular-season results completed before October 15. Exhibitions are excluded.","Player totals use the available box scores and may be incomplete. The Hec Crighton Watch is CanUFootball’s own list."],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-16","label":"Official national schedule"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260905_gdvt.xml","label":"September 5 · Saskatchewan at Manitoba"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260911_hvcf.xml","label":"September 11 · Manitoba at Regina"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_96n6.xml","label":"September 19 · Calgary at Manitoba"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_ncut.xml","label":"September 26 · UBC at Manitoba"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261002_k48e.xml","label":"October 2 · Manitoba at Alberta"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260911_j4p4.xml","label":"September 11 · Calgary at Saskatchewan"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260918_mge2.xml","label":"September 18 · Saskatchewan at Alberta"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_u9sf.xml","label":"September 26 · Saskatchewan at Regina"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261003_8tvd.xml","label":"October 3 · UBC at Saskatchewan"},{"url":"https://bearsandpandas.ca/sports/football/stats/2026/university-of-saskatchewan/boxscore/8948","label":"Anton Amundrud · player statistics"},{"url":"https://gobisons.ca/sports/football/stats/2026/saskatchewan-huskies/boxscore/9300","label":"Anton Amundrud · player statistics"},{"url":"https://godinos.com/sports/football/stats/2026/saskatchewan/boxscore/15527","label":"Anton Amundrud · player statistics"},{"url":"https://huskies.usask.ca/sports/football/stats/2026-27/regina-rams/boxscore/6998","label":"Anton Amundrud · player statistics"},{"url":"https://huskies.usask.ca/sports/football/stats/2026-27/ubc-thunderbirds/boxscore/6999","label":"Anton Amundrud · player statistics"},{"url":"https://huskies.usask.ca/news/2026/10/15/football-no-3-huskies-eye-postseason-clinch-in-rematch-with-manitoba.aspx","label":"Saskatchewan Huskies · pregame reporting"}]},{"id":"2026-10-17-bishops-sherbrooke","away":"bishops","home":"sherbrooke","date":"2026-10-17","conference":"RSEQ","asOf":"2026-10-15","title":"Gaiters, Vert & Or look for a much-needed win","paragraphs":["Sherbrooke came within six points of Montréal in its last game. The Vert & Or now need to turn a competitive afternoon into something they have not had this season: a win.","Bishop's visits Saturday with problems of its own. The Gaiters are 1–4 and have lost their last three, most recently a 47–27 game against McGill. Sherbrooke is 0–5 after its 23–17 loss to the Carabins.","For the Vert & Or, that was a considerably better showing than the previous two weeks. Laval beat them 55–24, and McGill followed with a 34–1 win. Holding Montréal to 23 gave Sherbrooke a chance to stay in the game.","Bishop's has struggled to score consistently too. The Gaiters managed nine points against Montréal and five against Concordia before putting up 27 in the loss to McGill.","Neither side has averaged 17 points a game, while both have allowed considerably more. That makes this an opportunity for two offences that have spent much of the season trying to keep pace.","Sherbrooke needs to carry its improved defensive effort into another week. Bishop's needs to pair its better scoring output with more stops. Whichever team manages both will have a good chance to leave with a much-needed result."],"notes":["Records and team scoring use regular-season results completed before October 15. Exhibitions are excluded.","Player totals use the available box scores and may be incomplete. The Hec Crighton Watch is CanUFootball’s own list."],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-17","label":"Official national schedule"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260905_v7ru.xml","label":"September 5 · McGill at Bishop's"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-09-12","label":"September 12 · Sherbrooke at Bishop's"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260918_lxef.xml","label":"September 18 · Bishop's at Montréal"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_shbp.xml","label":"September 26 · Concordia at Bishop's"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261004_7x1b.xml","label":"October 4 · Bishop's at McGill"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-09-04","label":"September 4 · Montréal at Sherbrooke"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_yf7q.xml","label":"September 19 · Sherbrooke at Laval"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_8v74.xml","label":"September 26 · McGill at Sherbrooke"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-03","label":"October 3 · Sherbrooke at Montréal"}]},{"id":"2026-10-17-carleton-laurier","away":"carleton","home":"laurier","date":"2026-10-17","conference":"OUA","asOf":"2026-10-15","title":"Ravens chase first win on road at Laurier","paragraphs":["Carleton was three points from a win against Ottawa. A week later, Western made sure there would be no close finish.","The Ravens now head to Laurier looking for their first victory after a 49–7 loss to the Mustangs dropped them to 0–6. Their 35–32 loss to the Gee-Gees showed they can make a game of it, but they have not been able to turn those chances into a win.","Laurier is trying to recover from its own setback. The Golden Hawks lost 39–31 to Waterloo on October 3, leaving them 2–4 after a stretch that also included an 18–16 loss to McMaster and a 36–13 win over York.","The Ravens have been able to score more often than their record might suggest, averaging 21.8 points. Keeping opponents off the scoreboard has been the bigger problem: Carleton is allowing 44.2 a game.","That gives Laurier an obvious opening. The Golden Hawks average 28.5 points, but their own defence has allowed 27.7, and Waterloo showed what can happen when an opponent keeps answering.","Carleton needs to bring the offence it showed against Ottawa and a much better defensive effort than it managed against Western. Laurier needs to make sure the Ravens do not get another chance to hang around until the final minutes."],"notes":["Records and team scoring use regular-season results completed before October 15. Exhibitions are excluded.","Player totals use the available box scores and may be incomplete. The Hec Crighton Watch is CanUFootball’s own list."],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-17","label":"Official national schedule"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260829_y7d5.xml","label":"August 29 · Carleton at York"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260906_o8yt.xml","label":"September 6 · Waterloo at Carleton"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260912_jbsa.xml","label":"September 12 · Carleton at Guelph"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_o7bu.xml","label":"September 19 · Queen's at Carleton"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261004_yqpv.xml","label":"October 4 · Carleton at Ottawa"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261010_e02s.xml","label":"October 10 · Western at Carleton"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260829_zyoz.xml","label":"August 29 · Guelph at Laurier"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260906_tqi8.xml","label":"September 6 · Laurier at Windsor"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-09-12","label":"September 12 · Ottawa at Laurier"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_r1pc.xml","label":"September 19 · Laurier at McMaster"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_onmm.xml","label":"September 26 · York at Laurier"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261003_3xzq.xml","label":"October 3 · Laurier at Waterloo"}]},{"id":"2026-10-17-guelph-queens","away":"guelph","home":"queens","date":"2026-10-17","conference":"OUA","asOf":"2026-10-15","title":"Gaels look to rebound as Gryphons visit Kingston","paragraphs":["Queen's lost its unbeaten record last week. The schedule offers little time to dwell on it.","Guelph brings a three-game winning streak to Kingston on Saturday, giving the Gaels another difficult OUA matchup after their 25–22 loss to Windsor. Queen's is 5–1; a Gryphons win would leave both teams with five victories.","Guelph has scored 124 points during its winning run, beating Ottawa 31–28, Waterloo 47–22 and Toronto 46–0. The Gryphons have also allowed fewer than 20 points a game over the season, giving them more than one way to stay in a contest.","Queen's had scored 41 points in consecutive wins over Ottawa and Western before Windsor held the Gaels to 22. The loss did not erase what has been a productive offence, but it did show that Queen's can be kept within reach.","The quarterbacks give this game another reason to watch. Alex Vreeken has thrown for 1,872 yards in the five games included in the site's player totals, while Guelph's Tristan Aboud has 1,722 in six. Both appear on CanUFootball's Hec Crighton Watch.","The Gaels average 39.3 points a game and the Gryphons 37.2. Guelph has the lower points-against average. Queen's will want to get its offence moving again early; the Gryphons will try to make the Gaels work for the kind of scoring they found before the Windsor game."],"notes":["Records and team scoring use regular-season results completed before October 15. Exhibitions are excluded.","Player totals use the available box scores and may be incomplete. The Hec Crighton Watch is CanUFootball’s own list."],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-17","label":"Official national schedule"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260829_zyoz.xml","label":"August 29 · Guelph at Laurier"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260906_zejw.xml","label":"September 6 · McMaster at Guelph"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260912_jbsa.xml","label":"September 12 · Carleton at Guelph"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_hkpj.xml","label":"September 19 · Guelph at Ottawa"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_pvm1.xml","label":"September 26 · Waterloo at Guelph"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261003_07bf.xml","label":"October 3 · Guelph at Toronto"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260830_q4gr.xml","label":"August 30 · Queen's at Toronto"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260912_pii8.xml","label":"September 12 · Waterloo at Queen's"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_o7bu.xml","label":"September 19 · Queen's at Carleton"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_2hsv.xml","label":"September 26 · Ottawa at Queen's"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261003_7san.xml","label":"October 3 · Queen's at Western"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261010_11lr.xml","label":"October 10 · Windsor at Queen's"},{"url":"https://gogaelsgo.com/sports/football/stats/2026-2027/carleton-ravens/boxscore/13808","label":"Alex Vreeken · player statistics"},{"url":"https://gogaelsgo.com/sports/football/stats/2026-2027/ottawa-gee-gees/boxscore/13809","label":"Alex Vreeken · player statistics"},{"url":"https://gogaelsgo.com/sports/football/stats/2026-2027/toronto-varsity-blues/boxscore/13806","label":"Alex Vreeken · player statistics"},{"url":"https://gogaelsgo.com/sports/football/stats/2026-2027/waterloo-warriors/boxscore/13807","label":"Alex Vreeken · player statistics"},{"url":"https://gogaelsgo.com/sports/football/stats/2026-2027/western-mustangs/boxscore/13810","label":"Alex Vreeken · player statistics"},{"url":"https://gryphons.ca/sports/football/stats/2026-27/carleton-ravens/boxscore/9559","label":"Tristan Aboud · player statistics"},{"url":"https://gryphons.ca/sports/football/stats/2026-27/laurier-golden-hawks/boxscore/9557","label":"Tristan Aboud · player statistics"},{"url":"https://gryphons.ca/sports/football/stats/2026-27/mcmaster-marauders/boxscore/9558","label":"Tristan Aboud · player statistics"},{"url":"https://gryphons.ca/sports/football/stats/2026-27/ottawa-gee-gees/boxscore/9560","label":"Tristan Aboud · player statistics"},{"url":"https://gryphons.ca/sports/football/stats/2026-27/toronto-varsity-blues/boxscore/9562","label":"Tristan Aboud · player statistics"}]},{"id":"2026-10-17-mcmaster-waterloo","away":"mcmaster","home":"waterloo","date":"2026-10-17","conference":"OUA","asOf":"2026-10-15","title":"Marauders take stingy defence into Waterloo","paragraphs":["Waterloo found enough offence to beat Laurier in its last game. Finding that much room against McMaster will be another matter.","The Marauders visit Saturday at 5–1, with a defence allowing just 15.7 points a game. They held Toronto to six in a 26–6 win on October 9 and have made a habit of keeping games manageable for their offence.","Waterloo is coming off a 39–31 win over Laurier, a welcome response after losses to Windsor and Guelph. The Warriors were outscored 91–40 in those two games before turning the result around against the Golden Hawks.","Their offence has averaged 26.7 points, slightly more than McMaster's 24.2. The difference between the teams has been at the other end: Waterloo has allowed 39.2 points a game, leaving the Warriors with far more work to do when they have the ball.","McMaster has already shown it can win a close one, edging Laurier 18–16 before losing 32–25 to Western. The Marauders do not need a high-scoring game to be comfortable.","That puts the pressure on Waterloo to get stops as well as points. Another good offensive afternoon would help, but asking the Warriors to keep answering against this McMaster defence would be a much harder route to a win."],"notes":["Records and team scoring use regular-season results completed before October 15. Exhibitions are excluded.","Player totals use the available box scores and may be incomplete. The Hec Crighton Watch is CanUFootball’s own list."],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-17","label":"Official national schedule"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260829_uxji.xml","label":"August 29 · Windsor at McMaster"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260906_zejw.xml","label":"September 6 · McMaster at Guelph"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260912_y44l.xml","label":"September 12 · McMaster at York"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_r1pc.xml","label":"September 19 · Laurier at McMaster"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_xfxk.xml","label":"September 26 · McMaster at Western"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261009_44ma.xml","label":"October 9 · Toronto at McMaster"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260829_rmtf.xml","label":"August 29 · Ottawa at Waterloo"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260906_o8yt.xml","label":"September 6 · Waterloo at Carleton"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260912_pii8.xml","label":"September 12 · Waterloo at Queen's"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_ed0b.xml","label":"September 19 · Windsor at Waterloo"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_pvm1.xml","label":"September 26 · Waterloo at Guelph"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261003_3xzq.xml","label":"October 3 · Laurier at Waterloo"}]},{"id":"2026-10-17-saint-marys-acadia","away":"saint-marys","home":"acadia","date":"2026-10-17","conference":"AUS","asOf":"2026-10-15","title":"Unbeaten Huskies visit Axemen in AUS rematch","paragraphs":["Acadia knows what it is up against. Saint Mary's has already beaten the Axemen twice, and neither game gave Acadia enough offence to threaten for long.","The unbeaten Huskies visit Saturday at 5–0 after winning those meetings 29–16 and 24–7. The second came on October 2 and left the Axemen 1–4, with a 38–12 loss to StFX between the two Saint Mary's games.","The Huskies have allowed just 12.2 points a game. That has given their offence room to work without asking it to win a shootout every week, and they have scored 24 or more in each of their last three games.","Running back Malcolm Bussey is one of the players Acadia has to account for. He has 428 rushing yards in the four games included in CanUFootball's player totals and is on the site's Hec Crighton Watch.","Acadia has averaged 14.4 points while allowing 27.2. The Axemen need to keep drives going long enough to give their defence a break, then make more of the chances that do reach scoring range.","Saint Mary's has already shown it can control this matchup. For Acadia to change the result, it will need more than another solid stretch or two. It needs an offence that can keep the Huskies under pressure for the afternoon."],"notes":["Records and team scoring use regular-season results completed before October 15. Exhibitions are excluded.","Player totals use the available box scores and may be incomplete. The Hec Crighton Watch is CanUFootball’s own list."],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-17","label":"Official national schedule"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260905_olce.xml","label":"September 5 · Saint Mary's at StFX"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260911_aecb.xml","label":"September 11 · Mount Allison at Saint Mary's"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_vzdr.xml","label":"September 19 · Saint Mary's at Acadia"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_e8ye.xml","label":"September 26 · Saint Mary's at Mount Allison"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261002_b8gs.xml","label":"October 2 · Acadia at Saint Mary's"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260904_m54m.xml","label":"September 4 · Acadia at Mount Allison"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260912_s8sj.xml","label":"September 12 · Acadia at StFX"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_6175.xml","label":"September 26 · StFX at Acadia"}]},{"id":"2026-10-17-stfx-mount-allison","away":"stfx","home":"mount-allison","date":"2026-10-17","conference":"AUS","asOf":"2026-10-15","title":"Mounties look for answers against surging X-Men","paragraphs":["Mount Allison has had two recent chances to slow StFX. Neither went well.","The X-Men beat the Mounties 42–6 on September 19 and 44–14 on October 3. They meet again Saturday, with StFX at 3–2 and Mount Allison looking to improve on a 1–4 start.","StFX has won three straight, scoring 124 points while allowing 32. A 38–12 win over Acadia sits between those two Mount Allison games, giving the X-Men a run of results that has been convincing on both sides of the ball.","The Mounties did give Saint Mary's a closer game between their losses to StFX, falling 24–17. That result shows a better defensive afternoon is within reach, but Mount Allison has not brought the same resistance to this matchup.","StFX averages 30 points a game and allows 15.8. The Mounties are scoring 15.4 while giving up 32.8, leaving them with a difficult combination against an opponent that has already found plenty of scoring room.","Mount Allison needs to make the X-Men earn longer drives and keep its own offence on the field. If StFX is allowed to set the pace again, the Mounties have already seen how quickly this game can get away from them."],"notes":["Records and team scoring use regular-season results completed before October 15. Exhibitions are excluded.","Player totals use the available box scores and may be incomplete. The Hec Crighton Watch is CanUFootball’s own list."],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-17","label":"Official national schedule"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260905_olce.xml","label":"September 5 · Saint Mary's at StFX"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260912_s8sj.xml","label":"September 12 · Acadia at StFX"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_2r1j.xml","label":"September 19 · StFX at Mount Allison"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_6175.xml","label":"September 26 · StFX at Acadia"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261003_n4x7.xml","label":"October 3 · Mount Allison at StFX"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260904_m54m.xml","label":"September 4 · Acadia at Mount Allison"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260911_aecb.xml","label":"September 11 · Mount Allison at Saint Mary's"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_e8ye.xml","label":"September 26 · Saint Mary's at Mount Allison"}]},{"id":"2026-10-17-western-ottawa","away":"western","home":"ottawa","date":"2026-10-17","conference":"OUA","asOf":"2026-10-15","title":"Gee-Gees face Western after setback against York","paragraphs":["Ottawa could use a bounce-back game. Western is not an inviting opponent for one.","The Gee-Gees host the Mustangs after losing 19–12 to York, a result that left Ottawa 4–3. Western arrives at 5–1 after beating Carleton 49–7, quickly answering its own loss to Queen's.","The Mustangs are averaging 49 points a game. Even in their 41–30 loss to the Gaels, they produced enough offence to make a game of it. The following week, Carleton could not keep up.","Ottawa has had a more uneven stretch. A 41–20 loss to Queen's was followed by a 35–32 win over Carleton before York held the Gee-Gees to 12. Another quiet offensive day would leave Ottawa with a great deal to ask of its defence.","Western's Jerome Rancourt is on CanUFootball's Hec Crighton Watch, with 1,516 passing yards in the six games included in the site's player totals. The Mustangs' scoring has given opponents little room for empty possessions.","The Gee-Gees average 28.1 points and allow 24.6. They need to make Western work for its points while finding more of their own. Letting the Mustangs turn this into a race would be a demanding way to try to recover from the York loss."],"notes":["Records and team scoring use regular-season results completed before October 15. Exhibitions are excluded.","Player totals use the available box scores and may be incomplete. The Hec Crighton Watch is CanUFootball’s own list."],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-17","label":"Official national schedule"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260906_bmmb.xml","label":"September 6 · York at Western"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260912_nlwf.xml","label":"September 12 · Western at Windsor"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_qrnw.xml","label":"September 19 · Western at Toronto"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_xfxk.xml","label":"September 26 · McMaster at Western"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261003_7san.xml","label":"October 3 · Queen's at Western"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261010_e02s.xml","label":"October 10 · Western at Carleton"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260829_rmtf.xml","label":"August 29 · Ottawa at Waterloo"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260905_kxlu.xml","label":"September 5 · Toronto at Ottawa"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-09-12","label":"September 12 · Ottawa at Laurier"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_hkpj.xml","label":"September 19 · Guelph at Ottawa"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_2hsv.xml","label":"September 26 · Ottawa at Queen's"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261004_yqpv.xml","label":"October 4 · Carleton at Ottawa"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-10","label":"October 10 · Ottawa at York"},{"url":"https://gogaelsgo.com/sports/football/stats/2026-2027/western-mustangs/boxscore/13810","label":"Jerome Rancourt · player statistics"},{"url":"https://golancers.ca/sports/football/stats/2026/western-mustangs/boxscore/6119","label":"Jerome Rancourt · player statistics"},{"url":"https://marauders.ca/sports/football/stats/2026/western-university/boxscore/14057","label":"Jerome Rancourt · player statistics"},{"url":"https://varsityblues.ca/sports/football/stats/2026/western-university/boxscore/12855","label":"Jerome Rancourt · player statistics"},{"url":"https://westernmustangs.ca/sports/football/stats/2026-27/york-lions/boxscore/17092","label":"Jerome Rancourt · player statistics"}]},{"id":"2026-10-17-york-toronto","away":"york","home":"toronto","date":"2026-10-17","conference":"OUA","asOf":"2026-10-15","title":"Lions seek another win as Blues look for breakthrough","paragraphs":["York is coming off a win worth building on. Toronto is still trying to find one.","The Lions beat Ottawa 19–12 last week to move to 2–4, giving them a chance to put together consecutive victories when they face the Varsity Blues on Saturday.","For York, that was a sharp change from the previous two games. Laurier beat the Lions 36–13, then Windsor followed with a 51–2 win. Holding Ottawa to 12 gave York an afternoon in which its offence did not have to chase a large deficit.","Toronto has not found that balance. The Blues are 0–6 and have scored just six points in their last three games, losing 54–0 to Windsor, 46–0 to Guelph and 26–6 to McMaster.","The season averages tell much the same story. Toronto has scored four points a game while allowing 43.2. York has produced more offence, but its 13.2-point average leaves little room for complacency against anyone.","The Lions need to carry their defensive effort against Ottawa into another week. Toronto needs an offence that can sustain drives and turn field position into points. For the Blues, simply keeping the score close will not solve the problem if they cannot finish possessions."],"notes":["Records and team scoring use regular-season results completed before October 15. Exhibitions are excluded.","Player totals use the available box scores and may be incomplete. The Hec Crighton Watch is CanUFootball’s own list."],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-17","label":"Official national schedule"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260829_y7d5.xml","label":"August 29 · Carleton at York"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260906_bmmb.xml","label":"September 6 · York at Western"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260912_y44l.xml","label":"September 12 · McMaster at York"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_onmm.xml","label":"September 26 · York at Laurier"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261003_dr1h.xml","label":"October 3 · York at Windsor"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-10","label":"October 10 · Ottawa at York"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260830_q4gr.xml","label":"August 30 · Queen's at Toronto"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260905_kxlu.xml","label":"September 5 · Toronto at Ottawa"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_qrnw.xml","label":"September 19 · Western at Toronto"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_1coy.xml","label":"September 26 · Toronto at Windsor"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261003_07bf.xml","label":"October 3 · Guelph at Toronto"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261009_44ma.xml","label":"October 9 · Toronto at McMaster"}]},{"id":"2026-10-18-mcgill-laval","away":"mcgill","home":"laval","date":"2026-10-18","conference":"RSEQ","asOf":"2026-10-15","title":"McGill takes winning run into showdown with Laval","paragraphs":["McGill has won three straight. Extending that run will mean doing something no one has managed this regular season: beating Laval.","The Redbirds visit Sunday at 4–1 after wins over Concordia, Sherbrooke and Bishop's. Laval is 5–0 and has been just as convincing lately, scoring 145 points in its last three games.","McGill has not been short of offence either. The Redbirds beat Concordia 29–8, Sherbrooke 34–1 and Bishop's 47–27, giving them 110 points across the winning run. Their defence has allowed 17 points a game over the season, almost identical to Laval's 17.2.","Running back Jerry Momo is a big part of McGill's appeal in this matchup. He has rushed for 733 yards in the five games included in CanUFootball's totals and is on the site's Hec Crighton Watch. Keeping him productive would help the Redbirds avoid putting everything on their passing game.","Laval has averaged 39 points, compared with McGill's 29.6. The Rouge et Or beat Montréal 42–34 before handling Concordia 48–15, showing they can win a high-scoring contest as well as pull away from an opponent.","McGill needs its defence to keep Laval within reach and its offence to make the most of possessions. The Redbirds have earned their winning run; Sunday will show how it stands up against the unbeaten Rouge et Or."],"notes":["Records and team scoring use regular-season results completed before October 15. Exhibitions are excluded.","Player totals use the available box scores and may be incomplete. The Hec Crighton Watch is CanUFootball’s own list."],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-18","label":"Official national schedule"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260905_v7ru.xml","label":"September 5 · McGill at Bishop's"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260911_60uu.xml","label":"September 11 · Laval at McGill"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_hi62.xml","label":"September 19 · McGill at Concordia"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_8v74.xml","label":"September 26 · McGill at Sherbrooke"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261004_7x1b.xml","label":"October 4 · Bishop's at McGill"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-09-05","label":"September 5 · Concordia at Laval"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_yf7q.xml","label":"September 19 · Sherbrooke at Laval"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_3enl.xml","label":"September 26 · Montréal at Laval"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261003_xhzw.xml","label":"October 3 · Laval at Concordia"},{"url":"https://mcgillathletics.ca/sports/football/stats/2026-27/bishop-s/boxscore/12458","label":"Jerry Momo · player statistics"},{"url":"https://mcgillathletics.ca/sports/football/stats/2026-27/bishop-s/boxscore/12462","label":"Jerry Momo · player statistics"},{"url":"https://mcgillathletics.ca/sports/football/stats/2026-27/concordia-shaughnessy-cup-/boxscore/12460","label":"Jerry Momo · player statistics"},{"url":"https://mcgillathletics.ca/sports/football/stats/2026-27/laval-tva-/boxscore/12459","label":"Jerry Momo · player statistics"},{"url":"https://mcgillathletics.ca/sports/football/stats/2026-27/sherbrooke/boxscore/12461","label":"Jerry Momo · player statistics"}]},{"id":"2026-10-23-alberta-saskatchewan","away":"alberta","home":"saskatchewan","date":"2026-10-23","conference":"CW","asOf":"2026-10-15","title":"Golden Bears face return trip to Saskatchewan","paragraphs":["Alberta does not have to look far for a reminder of how difficult a visit to Saskatchewan can become. The Huskies won their September meeting 65–12.","The Golden Bears will need a much better defensive effort in the return game. Saskatchewan has averaged 40.6 points through its first five games, while Alberta has allowed 40.0.","There has been some encouragement for Alberta on offence. The Bears beat Calgary 42–35 on September 25, but followed it with an 18–3 loss to Manitoba. That inconsistency has left them at 1–4 heading into the final stretch of the schedule.","Saskatchewan has won four straight since its opening loss to Manitoba. Quarterback Anton Amundrud has thrown for 1,543 yards in the five games included in CanUFootball's player totals and appears on the site's Hec Crighton Watch.","Alberta needs to give its offence a chance to work without facing another large early deficit. Saskatchewan has already shown what it can do when the Golden Bears cannot slow the scoring. The return game will test whether Alberta can make the Huskies earn a different kind of win."],"notes":["Records and team scoring use regular-season results completed before October 15. Exhibitions are excluded.","Player totals use the available box scores and may be incomplete. The Hec Crighton Watch is CanUFootball’s own list."],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-23","label":"Official national schedule"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260904_pg8n.xml","label":"September 4 · Regina at Alberta"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260911_19fu.xml","label":"September 11 · Alberta at UBC"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260918_mge2.xml","label":"September 18 · Saskatchewan at Alberta"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260925_jbqx.xml","label":"September 25 · Alberta at Calgary"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261002_k48e.xml","label":"October 2 · Manitoba at Alberta"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260905_gdvt.xml","label":"September 5 · Saskatchewan at Manitoba"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260911_j4p4.xml","label":"September 11 · Calgary at Saskatchewan"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_u9sf.xml","label":"September 26 · Saskatchewan at Regina"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261003_8tvd.xml","label":"October 3 · UBC at Saskatchewan"},{"url":"https://bearsandpandas.ca/sports/football/stats/2026/university-of-saskatchewan/boxscore/8948","label":"Anton Amundrud · player statistics"},{"url":"https://gobisons.ca/sports/football/stats/2026/saskatchewan-huskies/boxscore/9300","label":"Anton Amundrud · player statistics"},{"url":"https://godinos.com/sports/football/stats/2026/saskatchewan/boxscore/15527","label":"Anton Amundrud · player statistics"},{"url":"https://huskies.usask.ca/sports/football/stats/2026-27/regina-rams/boxscore/6998","label":"Anton Amundrud · player statistics"},{"url":"https://huskies.usask.ca/sports/football/stats/2026-27/ubc-thunderbirds/boxscore/6999","label":"Anton Amundrud · player statistics"}]},{"id":"2026-10-23-mount-allison-saint-marys","away":"mount-allison","home":"saint-marys","date":"2026-10-23","conference":"AUS","asOf":"2026-10-15","title":"Mounties take another run at Huskies","paragraphs":["Mount Allison stayed within a touchdown of Saint Mary's in September. The Mounties will want more than a close result when they get another chance against the Huskies.","Saint Mary's won that meeting 24–17 on September 26. It was a competitive game in a season that has otherwise been difficult for Mount Allison, which is 1–4 through its first five outings.","The Mounties have averaged 15.4 points while allowing 32.8. Against a Saint Mary's defence allowing just 12.2, they will have to make scoring chances count rather than rely on getting many of them.","The Huskies are 5–0 and have scored 24 or more in each of their last three games. Malcolm Bussey has given them a threat on the ground, rushing for 428 yards in the four games included in CanUFootball's player totals and making the site's Hec Crighton Watch.","Mount Allison already knows it can keep this matchup close. Finding the extra stop or scoring drive to change the result is the next step. Saint Mary's will try to avoid giving the Mounties another opportunity to stay in it until the end."],"notes":["Records and team scoring use regular-season results completed before October 15. Exhibitions are excluded.","Player totals use the available box scores and may be incomplete. The Hec Crighton Watch is CanUFootball’s own list."],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-23","label":"Official national schedule"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260904_m54m.xml","label":"September 4 · Acadia at Mount Allison"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260911_aecb.xml","label":"September 11 · Mount Allison at Saint Mary's"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_2r1j.xml","label":"September 19 · StFX at Mount Allison"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_e8ye.xml","label":"September 26 · Saint Mary's at Mount Allison"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261003_n4x7.xml","label":"October 3 · Mount Allison at StFX"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260905_olce.xml","label":"September 5 · Saint Mary's at StFX"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_vzdr.xml","label":"September 19 · Saint Mary's at Acadia"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261002_b8gs.xml","label":"October 2 · Acadia at Saint Mary's"}]},{"id":"2026-10-23-ubc-regina","away":"ubc","home":"regina","date":"2026-10-23","conference":"CW","asOf":"2026-10-15","title":"Thunderbirds, Rams meet again after close finish","paragraphs":["Regina was five points short the last time it played UBC. The Rams will get another chance to close that gap when the Thunderbirds visit.","UBC won the September 18 meeting 25–20. For Regina, it was the start of a three-game stretch of close losses, followed by a 38–31 defeat against Saskatchewan and a 14–13 loss to Calgary.","The Rams have allowed just 18.6 points a game through five outings. That has kept them in games, but at 2–3 they need to turn more of those opportunities into wins.","UBC is 3–2 over the same period. The Thunderbirds beat Manitoba 31–6 before losing 34–24 to Saskatchewan, with their running game offering a consistent threat. Marvyn Larozar has 713 rushing yards in the four games included in CanUFootball's totals and is on the Hec Crighton Watch.","Regina needs to limit that ground game without leaving easy opportunities elsewhere. UBC, which averages 26 points to Regina's 25.2, has little reason to expect an easy afternoon after the teams' first meeting stayed so close."],"notes":["Records and team scoring use regular-season results completed before October 15. Exhibitions are excluded.","Player totals use the available box scores and may be incomplete. The Hec Crighton Watch is CanUFootball’s own list."],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-23","label":"Official national schedule"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260904_bx7n.xml","label":"September 4 · UBC at Calgary"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260911_19fu.xml","label":"September 11 · Alberta at UBC"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260918_y81r.xml","label":"September 18 · Regina at UBC"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_ncut.xml","label":"September 26 · UBC at Manitoba"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261003_8tvd.xml","label":"October 3 · UBC at Saskatchewan"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260904_pg8n.xml","label":"September 4 · Regina at Alberta"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260911_hvcf.xml","label":"September 11 · Manitoba at Regina"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_u9sf.xml","label":"September 26 · Saskatchewan at Regina"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261003_hww9.xml","label":"October 3 · Regina at Calgary"},{"url":"https://bearsandpandas.ca/sports/football/stats/2026/university-of-british-columbia/boxscore/8947","label":"Marvyn Larozar · player statistics"},{"url":"https://gobisons.ca/sports/football/stats/2026/ubc-thunderbirds/boxscore/9303","label":"Marvyn Larozar · player statistics"},{"url":"https://huskies.usask.ca/sports/football/stats/2026-27/ubc-thunderbirds/boxscore/6999","label":"Marvyn Larozar · player statistics"},{"url":"https://www.reginacougars.com/sports/football/stats/2026/ubc/boxscore/11425","label":"Marvyn Larozar · player statistics"}]},{"id":"2026-10-24-acadia-stfx","away":"acadia","home":"stfx","date":"2026-10-24","conference":"AUS","asOf":"2026-10-15","title":"Axemen seek better result against X-Men","paragraphs":["Acadia will have to find a way to slow StFX before worrying about how to outscore it.","The X-Men won their September meeting 38–12 and have scored 124 points across their last three games. Two wins over Mount Allison came on either side of that Acadia result, giving StFX a convincing run heading into the later part of the AUS schedule.","The Axemen are 1–4 through five games and have been held to 16 points or fewer in each of their last three. They lost 29–16 and 24–7 to Saint Mary's around the defeat against StFX.","That leaves Acadia with work to do on offence as well as defence. The Axemen average 14.4 points a game; StFX has allowed only 15.8 while scoring 30.0.","Longer drives would give Acadia's defence a break and reduce the number of chances for the X-Men to pull away. StFX will try to make the rematch follow the first game, when its offence produced more points than the Axemen could answer."],"notes":["Records and team scoring use regular-season results completed before October 15. Exhibitions are excluded.","Player totals use the available box scores and may be incomplete. The Hec Crighton Watch is CanUFootball’s own list."],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-24","label":"Official national schedule"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260904_m54m.xml","label":"September 4 · Acadia at Mount Allison"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260912_s8sj.xml","label":"September 12 · Acadia at StFX"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_vzdr.xml","label":"September 19 · Saint Mary's at Acadia"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_6175.xml","label":"September 26 · StFX at Acadia"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261002_b8gs.xml","label":"October 2 · Acadia at Saint Mary's"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260905_olce.xml","label":"September 5 · Saint Mary's at StFX"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_2r1j.xml","label":"September 19 · StFX at Mount Allison"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261003_n4x7.xml","label":"October 3 · Mount Allison at StFX"}]},{"id":"2026-10-24-concordia-sherbrooke","away":"concordia","home":"sherbrooke","date":"2026-10-24","conference":"RSEQ","asOf":"2026-10-15","title":"Stingers, Vert & Or meet with offence under scrutiny","paragraphs":["Concordia needs points. Sherbrooke needs stops. Their meeting gives both a chance to address a problem that has followed them through much of the season.","The Stingers have scored 11 points a game through a 1–4 start. Their lone win came in a 10–5 game against Bishop's, while their last outing ended in a 48–15 loss to Laval.","Sherbrooke is 0–5, allowing 37 points a game. The Vert & Or did show improvement against Montréal, losing 23–17 after being beaten 55–24 by Laval and 34–1 by McGill.","That Montréal result gives Sherbrooke something to build on. Repeating the defensive effort would put pressure on a Concordia offence that has struggled to finish drives, but the Vert & Or still need enough points of their own.","Sherbrooke averages 16.4, only a little more than the Stingers. Neither team has made a habit of winning high-scoring games, and both would welcome an afternoon in which the offence gives the defence some breathing room."],"notes":["Records and team scoring use regular-season results completed before October 15. Exhibitions are excluded.","Player totals use the available box scores and may be incomplete. The Hec Crighton Watch is CanUFootball’s own list."],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-24","label":"Official national schedule"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-09-05","label":"September 5 · Concordia at Laval"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260912_ppda.xml","label":"September 12 · Montréal at Concordia"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_hi62.xml","label":"September 19 · McGill at Concordia"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_shbp.xml","label":"September 26 · Concordia at Bishop's"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261003_xhzw.xml","label":"October 3 · Laval at Concordia"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-09-04","label":"September 4 · Montréal at Sherbrooke"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-09-12","label":"September 12 · Sherbrooke at Bishop's"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_yf7q.xml","label":"September 19 · Sherbrooke at Laval"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_8v74.xml","label":"September 26 · McGill at Sherbrooke"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-03","label":"October 3 · Sherbrooke at Montréal"}]},{"id":"2026-10-24-laurier-western","away":"laurier","home":"western","date":"2026-10-24","conference":"OUA","asOf":"2026-10-15","title":"Golden Hawks face high-scoring Mustangs","paragraphs":["Laurier cannot count on keeping pace with Western simply by trading scores. The Mustangs have made that a demanding proposition for almost everyone they have played.","Western has averaged 49 points through a 5–1 start. Its last three games included a 32–25 win over McMaster, a 41–30 loss to Queen's and a 49–7 win over Carleton.","The Golden Hawks are 2–4 after losing 39–31 to Waterloo. They beat York 36–13 before that, but a narrow 18–16 loss to McMaster earlier in the stretch shows how little has separated some of Laurier's results.","Defensively, Laurier has allowed 27.7 points a game. Western has been held below that figure infrequently enough to make this a substantial test for the Golden Hawks.","Jerome Rancourt has thrown for 1,516 yards in the six games included in CanUFootball's player totals and is on the site's Hec Crighton Watch. Laurier needs to keep Western's offence from dictating the game, then turn its own possessions into points. Long stretches without either would give the Mustangs too much room."],"notes":["Records and team scoring use regular-season results completed before October 15. Exhibitions are excluded.","Player totals use the available box scores and may be incomplete. The Hec Crighton Watch is CanUFootball’s own list."],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-24","label":"Official national schedule"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260829_zyoz.xml","label":"August 29 · Guelph at Laurier"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260906_tqi8.xml","label":"September 6 · Laurier at Windsor"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-09-12","label":"September 12 · Ottawa at Laurier"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_r1pc.xml","label":"September 19 · Laurier at McMaster"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_onmm.xml","label":"September 26 · York at Laurier"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261003_3xzq.xml","label":"October 3 · Laurier at Waterloo"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260906_bmmb.xml","label":"September 6 · York at Western"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260912_nlwf.xml","label":"September 12 · Western at Windsor"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_qrnw.xml","label":"September 19 · Western at Toronto"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_xfxk.xml","label":"September 26 · McMaster at Western"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261003_7san.xml","label":"October 3 · Queen's at Western"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261010_e02s.xml","label":"October 10 · Western at Carleton"},{"url":"https://gogaelsgo.com/sports/football/stats/2026-2027/western-mustangs/boxscore/13810","label":"Jerome Rancourt · player statistics"},{"url":"https://golancers.ca/sports/football/stats/2026/western-mustangs/boxscore/6119","label":"Jerome Rancourt · player statistics"},{"url":"https://marauders.ca/sports/football/stats/2026/western-university/boxscore/14057","label":"Jerome Rancourt · player statistics"},{"url":"https://varsityblues.ca/sports/football/stats/2026/western-university/boxscore/12855","label":"Jerome Rancourt · player statistics"},{"url":"https://westernmustangs.ca/sports/football/stats/2026-27/york-lions/boxscore/17092","label":"Jerome Rancourt · player statistics"}]},{"id":"2026-10-24-laval-bishops","away":"laval","home":"bishops","date":"2026-10-24","conference":"RSEQ","asOf":"2026-10-15","title":"Gaiters prepare for another test against Laval","paragraphs":["Bishop's has spent much of the season trying to keep opponents within reach. Laval brings an offence that can make that a difficult task in a hurry.","The Rouge et Or have averaged 39 points through a 5–0 start. They scored 55 against Sherbrooke, 42 against Montréal and 48 against Concordia in their last three games.","The Gaiters are 1–4, averaging 14.8 points and allowing 26.8. Their offence improved in a 47–27 loss to McGill, but the extra points did not come with enough stops to change the result.","Bishop's had managed only nine points against Montréal and five against Concordia in its previous two outings. Another afternoon like that would give Laval's offence little pressure to deal with.","Victor Charland has thrown for 1,267 yards in the five games included in CanUFootball's player totals. He and receiver Olivier Cool appear on the site's Hec Crighton Watch, adding to the threats Bishop's must account for.","The Gaiters need to keep the ball, finish drives and make Laval work for its scoring chances. The Rouge et Or have shown they can pile up points when an opponent cannot do those things together."],"notes":["Records and team scoring use regular-season results completed before October 15. Exhibitions are excluded.","Player totals use the available box scores and may be incomplete. The Hec Crighton Watch is CanUFootball’s own list."],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-24","label":"Official national schedule"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-09-05","label":"September 5 · Concordia at Laval"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260911_60uu.xml","label":"September 11 · Laval at McGill"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_yf7q.xml","label":"September 19 · Sherbrooke at Laval"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_3enl.xml","label":"September 26 · Montréal at Laval"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261003_xhzw.xml","label":"October 3 · Laval at Concordia"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260905_v7ru.xml","label":"September 5 · McGill at Bishop's"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-09-12","label":"September 12 · Sherbrooke at Bishop's"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260918_lxef.xml","label":"September 18 · Bishop's at Montréal"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_shbp.xml","label":"September 26 · Concordia at Bishop's"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261004_7x1b.xml","label":"October 4 · Bishop's at McGill"},{"url":"https://mcgillathletics.ca/sports/football/stats/2026-27/laval-tva-/boxscore/12459","label":"Victor Charland · player statistics"},{"url":"https://rougeetor.ulaval.ca/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/boxscore-20260905-concordia-laval.pdf","label":"Victor Charland · player statistics"}]},{"id":"2026-10-24-manitoba-calgary","away":"manitoba","home":"calgary","date":"2026-10-24","conference":"CW","asOf":"2026-10-15","title":"Dinos, Bisons set for rematch after two-point game","paragraphs":["Calgary was two points short against Manitoba in September. The Dinos get another chance after a first meeting that offered little comfort to either defence.","The Bisons won 38–36 on September 19. Since then, Manitoba has lost 31–6 to UBC and beaten Alberta 18–3, showing just how different its games can look from one week to the next.","Calgary also had a change of pace after that meeting. The Dinos lost 42–35 to Alberta before edging Regina 14–13, finding a win without needing the sort of scoring that had not been enough in the previous two games.","Through five outings, Calgary is 2–3 and averaging 28.2 points. Manitoba is 3–2, scoring 22 and allowing 23 a game.","The Dinos know they can move the score against the Bisons. What they need is a better result when Manitoba has the ball. One more stop could have changed the first meeting; the return game gives Calgary a chance to find it, while the Bisons will look to avoid needing another 38-point afternoon."],"notes":["Records and team scoring use regular-season results completed before October 15. Exhibitions are excluded.","Player totals use the available box scores and may be incomplete. The Hec Crighton Watch is CanUFootball’s own list."],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-24","label":"Official national schedule"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260905_gdvt.xml","label":"September 5 · Saskatchewan at Manitoba"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260911_hvcf.xml","label":"September 11 · Manitoba at Regina"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_96n6.xml","label":"September 19 · Calgary at Manitoba"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_ncut.xml","label":"September 26 · UBC at Manitoba"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261002_k48e.xml","label":"October 2 · Manitoba at Alberta"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260904_bx7n.xml","label":"September 4 · UBC at Calgary"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260911_j4p4.xml","label":"September 11 · Calgary at Saskatchewan"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260925_jbqx.xml","label":"September 25 · Alberta at Calgary"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261003_hww9.xml","label":"October 3 · Regina at Calgary"}]},{"id":"2026-10-24-montreal-mcgill","away":"montreal","home":"mcgill","date":"2026-10-24","conference":"RSEQ","asOf":"2026-10-15","title":"Carabins, Redbirds bring contrasting strengths to rematch","paragraphs":["Montréal has been scoring more. McGill has been giving up less. Their meeting puts those strengths directly against each other.","The teams are both 4–1 through five games, with Montréal averaging 38.8 points and McGill allowing 17.0. The Carabins have not been quite as comfortable defensively, giving up 22.2 a game.","McGill has won three straight, beating Concordia 29–8, Sherbrooke 34–1 and Bishop's 47–27. The Redbirds have found plenty of offence during that run, even if their season scoring average of 29.6 remains below Montréal's.","Running back Jerry Momo has rushed for 733 yards in the five games included in CanUFootball's totals and appears on the site's Hec Crighton Watch. A productive afternoon from him would help McGill control possession and keep the Carabins waiting for their next drive.","Montréal beat Sherbrooke 23–17 after losing 42–34 to Laval. The Carabins have shown they can win a close, lower-scoring game, but McGill will try to make them work for every possession. The Redbirds' defence has been a reason for their strong start; this is another chance to prove it."],"notes":["Records and team scoring use regular-season results completed before October 15. Exhibitions are excluded.","Player totals use the available box scores and may be incomplete. The Hec Crighton Watch is CanUFootball’s own list."],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-24","label":"Official national schedule"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-09-04","label":"September 4 · Montréal at Sherbrooke"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260912_ppda.xml","label":"September 12 · Montréal at Concordia"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260918_lxef.xml","label":"September 18 · Bishop's at Montréal"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_3enl.xml","label":"September 26 · Montréal at Laval"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-03","label":"October 3 · Sherbrooke at Montréal"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260905_v7ru.xml","label":"September 5 · McGill at Bishop's"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260911_60uu.xml","label":"September 11 · Laval at McGill"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_hi62.xml","label":"September 19 · McGill at Concordia"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_8v74.xml","label":"September 26 · McGill at Sherbrooke"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261004_7x1b.xml","label":"October 4 · Bishop's at McGill"},{"url":"https://mcgillathletics.ca/sports/football/stats/2026-27/bishop-s/boxscore/12458","label":"Jerry Momo · player statistics"},{"url":"https://mcgillathletics.ca/sports/football/stats/2026-27/bishop-s/boxscore/12462","label":"Jerry Momo · player statistics"},{"url":"https://mcgillathletics.ca/sports/football/stats/2026-27/concordia-shaughnessy-cup-/boxscore/12460","label":"Jerry Momo · player statistics"},{"url":"https://mcgillathletics.ca/sports/football/stats/2026-27/laval-tva-/boxscore/12459","label":"Jerry Momo · player statistics"},{"url":"https://mcgillathletics.ca/sports/football/stats/2026-27/sherbrooke/boxscore/12461","label":"Jerry Momo · player statistics"}]},{"id":"2026-10-24-queens-mcmaster","away":"queens","home":"mcmaster","date":"2026-10-24","conference":"OUA","asOf":"2026-10-15","title":"Gaels offence meets Marauders defence","paragraphs":["Queen's has been scoring almost 40 points a game. McMaster has been allowing fewer than 16. Their meeting offers a good test of which strength holds up.","Both teams are 5–1 through six games, but they have reached that record in different ways. The Gaels average 39.3 points; the Marauders score 24.2 and have repeatedly kept opponents from forcing them into a high-scoring contest.","McMaster beat Laurier 18–16, lost 32–25 to Western and then held Toronto to six points in a 26–6 win. That last result fit the pattern of a defence that has allowed 15.7 points a game.","Queen's is coming off its first loss, a 25–22 result against Windsor. Before that, the Gaels scored 41 in consecutive wins over Ottawa and Western.","Quarterback Alex Vreeken has thrown for 1,872 yards in the five games included in CanUFootball's totals and is on the site's Hec Crighton Watch. The Gaels will want to give him room to get the offence moving again. McMaster will try to make each scoring drive take more work than Queen's is used to."],"notes":["Records and team scoring use regular-season results completed before October 15. Exhibitions are excluded.","Player totals use the available box scores and may be incomplete. The Hec Crighton Watch is CanUFootball’s own list."],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-24","label":"Official national schedule"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260830_q4gr.xml","label":"August 30 · Queen's at Toronto"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260912_pii8.xml","label":"September 12 · Waterloo at Queen's"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_o7bu.xml","label":"September 19 · Queen's at Carleton"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_2hsv.xml","label":"September 26 · Ottawa at Queen's"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261003_7san.xml","label":"October 3 · Queen's at Western"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261010_11lr.xml","label":"October 10 · Windsor at Queen's"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260829_uxji.xml","label":"August 29 · Windsor at McMaster"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260906_zejw.xml","label":"September 6 · McMaster at Guelph"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260912_y44l.xml","label":"September 12 · McMaster at York"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_r1pc.xml","label":"September 19 · Laurier at McMaster"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_xfxk.xml","label":"September 26 · McMaster at Western"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261009_44ma.xml","label":"October 9 · Toronto at McMaster"},{"url":"https://gogaelsgo.com/sports/football/stats/2026-2027/carleton-ravens/boxscore/13808","label":"Alex Vreeken · player statistics"},{"url":"https://gogaelsgo.com/sports/football/stats/2026-2027/ottawa-gee-gees/boxscore/13809","label":"Alex Vreeken · player statistics"},{"url":"https://gogaelsgo.com/sports/football/stats/2026-2027/toronto-varsity-blues/boxscore/13806","label":"Alex Vreeken · player statistics"},{"url":"https://gogaelsgo.com/sports/football/stats/2026-2027/waterloo-warriors/boxscore/13807","label":"Alex Vreeken · player statistics"},{"url":"https://gogaelsgo.com/sports/football/stats/2026-2027/western-mustangs/boxscore/13810","label":"Alex Vreeken · player statistics"}]},{"id":"2026-10-24-toronto-carleton","away":"toronto","home":"carleton","date":"2026-10-24","conference":"OUA","asOf":"2026-10-15","title":"Blues, Ravens search for better finish to OUA season","paragraphs":["Toronto has struggled to score. Carleton has struggled to keep opponents from scoring. Their meeting gives both teams a chance to change an unhappy pattern.","The Varsity Blues are 0–6 through six games, with just 24 points scored. Their last three outings produced losses of 54–0 to Windsor, 46–0 to Guelph and 26–6 to McMaster.","Carleton is also 0–6 but has found more offence, averaging 21.8 points. The Ravens took Ottawa to a 35–32 game before losing 49–7 to Western, a reminder of how quickly their defensive problems can undo their scoring.","The Ravens have allowed 44.2 points a game, a little more than Toronto's 43.2. Neither side has had much room to recover from mistakes once an opponent gets rolling.","For Toronto, the first job is turning a drive into points rather than another change of possession. Carleton needs to make the Blues earn those chances. Both teams would welcome a game in which one good stretch is followed by another, instead of being wiped out by the next score."],"notes":["Records and team scoring use regular-season results completed before October 15. Exhibitions are excluded.","Player totals use the available box scores and may be incomplete. The Hec Crighton Watch is CanUFootball’s own list."],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-24","label":"Official national schedule"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260830_q4gr.xml","label":"August 30 · Queen's at Toronto"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260905_kxlu.xml","label":"September 5 · Toronto at Ottawa"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_qrnw.xml","label":"September 19 · Western at Toronto"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_1coy.xml","label":"September 26 · Toronto at Windsor"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261003_07bf.xml","label":"October 3 · Guelph at Toronto"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261009_44ma.xml","label":"October 9 · Toronto at McMaster"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260829_y7d5.xml","label":"August 29 · Carleton at York"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260906_o8yt.xml","label":"September 6 · Waterloo at Carleton"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260912_jbsa.xml","label":"September 12 · Carleton at Guelph"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_o7bu.xml","label":"September 19 · Queen's at Carleton"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261004_yqpv.xml","label":"October 4 · Carleton at Ottawa"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261010_e02s.xml","label":"October 10 · Western at Carleton"}]},{"id":"2026-10-24-waterloo-york","away":"waterloo","home":"york","date":"2026-10-24","conference":"OUA","asOf":"2026-10-15","title":"Warriors, Lions look to build on recent wins","paragraphs":["Waterloo and York both have a recent win to build on. Their meeting will test whether either can turn that result into something more sustained.","The Warriors beat Laurier 39–31 in their last game. York answered losses to Laurier and Windsor by holding Ottawa to 12 points in a 19–12 win.","Both teams are 2–4 through six outings, but Waterloo has produced far more offence. The Warriors average 26.7 points, compared with York's 13.2.","The gap has been much smaller defensively. Waterloo has allowed 39.2 points a game and York 39.3, leaving both offences under pressure to make their possessions count.","York's effort against Ottawa offered a better route. The Lions did not need a huge scoring day because their defence kept the game under control. Repeating that against a Waterloo team coming off 39 points will take another good afternoon.","The Warriors will want to keep that offence moving while finding more stops of their own. York needs to avoid letting Waterloo's scoring turn this into a game the Lions have to chase."],"notes":["Records and team scoring use regular-season results completed before October 15. Exhibitions are excluded.","Player totals use the available box scores and may be incomplete. The Hec Crighton Watch is CanUFootball’s own list."],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-24","label":"Official national schedule"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260829_rmtf.xml","label":"August 29 · Ottawa at Waterloo"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260906_o8yt.xml","label":"September 6 · Waterloo at Carleton"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260912_pii8.xml","label":"September 12 · Waterloo at Queen's"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_ed0b.xml","label":"September 19 · Windsor at Waterloo"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_pvm1.xml","label":"September 26 · Waterloo at Guelph"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261003_3xzq.xml","label":"October 3 · Laurier at Waterloo"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260829_y7d5.xml","label":"August 29 · Carleton at York"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260906_bmmb.xml","label":"September 6 · York at Western"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260912_y44l.xml","label":"September 12 · McMaster at York"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_onmm.xml","label":"September 26 · York at Laurier"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261003_dr1h.xml","label":"October 3 · York at Windsor"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-10","label":"October 10 · Ottawa at York"}]},{"id":"2026-10-24-windsor-guelph","away":"windsor","home":"guelph","date":"2026-10-24","conference":"OUA","asOf":"2026-10-15","title":"Cotton, Aboud give Lancers-Gryphons plenty of intrigue","paragraphs":["Windsor and Guelph have both been scoring freely. Their quarterbacks give this OUA meeting another reason to pay attention.","Kareame Cotton has thrown for 2,113 yards in the seven games included in CanUFootball's player totals. Tristan Aboud has 1,722 in six for Guelph. Both are on the site's Hec Crighton Watch.","The Lancers are 5–2 after a 25–22 win over Queen's, a result that showed they can win a close game as well as a blowout. Windsor had beaten Toronto 54–0 and York 51–2 in its previous two outings.","Guelph is 4–2 and has won three straight, beating Ottawa 31–28, Waterloo 47–22 and Toronto 46–0. The Gryphons have averaged 37.2 points while allowing 19.7, giving them a defence capable of helping their offence rather than relying on it to do everything.","Windsor scores 40.7 a game and allows 22.0. There should be chances for both quarterbacks, but the team that gets more stops will have a much easier afternoon. Guelph will try to keep Cotton from settling in, while the Lancers need to prevent Aboud from extending the Gryphons' recent scoring run."],"notes":["Records and team scoring use regular-season results completed before October 15. Exhibitions are excluded.","Player totals use the available box scores and may be incomplete. The Hec Crighton Watch is CanUFootball’s own list."],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-24","label":"Official national schedule"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260829_uxji.xml","label":"August 29 · Windsor at McMaster"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260906_tqi8.xml","label":"September 6 · Laurier at Windsor"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260912_nlwf.xml","label":"September 12 · Western at Windsor"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_ed0b.xml","label":"September 19 · Windsor at Waterloo"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_1coy.xml","label":"September 26 · Toronto at Windsor"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261003_dr1h.xml","label":"October 3 · York at Windsor"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261010_11lr.xml","label":"October 10 · Windsor at Queen's"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260829_zyoz.xml","label":"August 29 · Guelph at Laurier"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260906_zejw.xml","label":"September 6 · McMaster at Guelph"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260912_jbsa.xml","label":"September 12 · Carleton at Guelph"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_hkpj.xml","label":"September 19 · Guelph at Ottawa"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_pvm1.xml","label":"September 26 · Waterloo at Guelph"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261003_07bf.xml","label":"October 3 · Guelph at Toronto"},{"url":"https://athletics.uwaterloo.ca/sports/football/stats/2026-27/windsor-lancers/boxscore/9407","label":"Kareame Cotton · player statistics"},{"url":"https://golancers.ca/sports/football/stats/2026/laurier-golden-hawks/boxscore/6118","label":"Kareame Cotton · player statistics"},{"url":"https://golancers.ca/sports/football/stats/2026/mcmaster-marauders/boxscore/6117","label":"Kareame Cotton · player statistics"},{"url":"https://golancers.ca/sports/football/stats/2026/toronto-varsity-blues/boxscore/6121","label":"Kareame Cotton · player statistics"},{"url":"https://golancers.ca/sports/football/stats/2026/western-mustangs/boxscore/6119","label":"Kareame Cotton · player statistics"},{"url":"https://golancers.ca/sports/football/stats/2026/york-lions/boxscore/6122","label":"Kareame Cotton · player statistics"},{"url":"https://gryphons.ca/sports/football/stats/2026-27/carleton-ravens/boxscore/9559","label":"Tristan Aboud · player statistics"},{"url":"https://gryphons.ca/sports/football/stats/2026-27/laurier-golden-hawks/boxscore/9557","label":"Tristan Aboud · player statistics"},{"url":"https://gryphons.ca/sports/football/stats/2026-27/mcmaster-marauders/boxscore/9558","label":"Tristan Aboud · player statistics"},{"url":"https://gryphons.ca/sports/football/stats/2026-27/ottawa-gee-gees/boxscore/9560","label":"Tristan Aboud · player statistics"},{"url":"https://gryphons.ca/sports/football/stats/2026-27/toronto-varsity-blues/boxscore/9562","label":"Tristan Aboud · player statistics"}]},{"id":"2026-10-30-saskatchewan-ubc","away":"saskatchewan","home":"ubc","date":"2026-10-30","conference":"CW","asOf":"2026-10-15","title":"Thunderbirds await return meeting with Huskies","paragraphs":["UBC had to leave Saskatoon with a loss the last time it faced Saskatchewan. The Thunderbirds get the return meeting at home as the Canada West regular season winds down.","The Huskies won 34–24 on October 3, extending a four-game winning streak. Through five games, Saskatchewan is 4–1 and averaging 40.6 points.","UBC is 3–2 over the same period. The Thunderbirds had won three straight before losing to the Huskies, including a 31–6 win over Manitoba that showed how difficult their defence can make an afternoon.","This game also brings two Hec Crighton Watch players together. Saskatchewan's Anton Amundrud has thrown for 1,543 yards in the five games included in CanUFootball's totals. UBC's Marvyn Larozar has rushed for 713 in four.","The Thunderbirds have allowed 20.4 points a game, but Saskatchewan found enough scoring to get past them in the first meeting. UBC needs to make the Huskies work harder for those points while keeping its own running game involved. Saskatchewan will look to make the return trip end the same way as the first game."],"notes":["Records and team scoring use regular-season results completed before October 15. Exhibitions are excluded.","Player totals use the available box scores and may be incomplete. The Hec Crighton Watch is CanUFootball’s own list."],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-30","label":"Official national schedule"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260905_gdvt.xml","label":"September 5 · Saskatchewan at Manitoba"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260911_j4p4.xml","label":"September 11 · Calgary at Saskatchewan"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260918_mge2.xml","label":"September 18 · Saskatchewan at Alberta"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_u9sf.xml","label":"September 26 · Saskatchewan at Regina"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261003_8tvd.xml","label":"October 3 · UBC at Saskatchewan"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260904_bx7n.xml","label":"September 4 · UBC at Calgary"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260911_19fu.xml","label":"September 11 · Alberta at UBC"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260918_y81r.xml","label":"September 18 · Regina at UBC"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_ncut.xml","label":"September 26 · UBC at Manitoba"},{"url":"https://bearsandpandas.ca/sports/football/stats/2026/university-of-british-columbia/boxscore/8947","label":"Marvyn Larozar · player statistics"},{"url":"https://gobisons.ca/sports/football/stats/2026/ubc-thunderbirds/boxscore/9303","label":"Marvyn Larozar · player statistics"},{"url":"https://huskies.usask.ca/sports/football/stats/2026-27/ubc-thunderbirds/boxscore/6999","label":"Marvyn Larozar · player statistics"},{"url":"https://www.reginacougars.com/sports/football/stats/2026/ubc/boxscore/11425","label":"Marvyn Larozar · player statistics"},{"url":"https://bearsandpandas.ca/sports/football/stats/2026/university-of-saskatchewan/boxscore/8948","label":"Anton Amundrud · player statistics"},{"url":"https://gobisons.ca/sports/football/stats/2026/saskatchewan-huskies/boxscore/9300","label":"Anton Amundrud · player statistics"},{"url":"https://godinos.com/sports/football/stats/2026/saskatchewan/boxscore/15527","label":"Anton Amundrud · player statistics"},{"url":"https://huskies.usask.ca/sports/football/stats/2026-27/regina-rams/boxscore/6998","label":"Anton Amundrud · player statistics"}]},{"id":"2026-10-30-sherbrooke-mcgill","away":"sherbrooke","home":"mcgill","date":"2026-10-30","conference":"RSEQ","asOf":"2026-10-15","title":"Vert & Or seek turnaround against Redbirds","paragraphs":["One point was all Sherbrooke managed against McGill in September. The return meeting will require a much different offensive effort.","The Redbirds won that game 34–1 and have put together three straight victories, also beating Concordia and Bishop's. McGill is 4–1 through five games, averaging 29.6 points while allowing 17.0.","Sherbrooke's next outing was more encouraging, a 23–17 loss to Montréal. The Vert & Or stayed within reach of the Carabins after losing heavily to Laval and McGill, but they are still looking for their first win at 0–5.","Stopping Jerry Momo is part of the assignment. The McGill running back has 733 rushing yards in the five games included in CanUFootball's totals and is on the site's Hec Crighton Watch.","Sherbrooke needs to get its offence off the field with points rather than empty possessions. A better defensive effort would help, but the Vert & Or cannot ask that unit to carry another game if the offence has as little to show for its work as it did in the first meeting."],"notes":["Records and team scoring use regular-season results completed before October 15. Exhibitions are excluded.","Player totals use the available box scores and may be incomplete. The Hec Crighton Watch is CanUFootball’s own list."],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-30","label":"Official national schedule"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-09-04","label":"September 4 · Montréal at Sherbrooke"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-09-12","label":"September 12 · Sherbrooke at Bishop's"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_yf7q.xml","label":"September 19 · Sherbrooke at Laval"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_8v74.xml","label":"September 26 · McGill at Sherbrooke"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-03","label":"October 3 · Sherbrooke at Montréal"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260905_v7ru.xml","label":"September 5 · McGill at Bishop's"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260911_60uu.xml","label":"September 11 · Laval at McGill"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_hi62.xml","label":"September 19 · McGill at Concordia"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261004_7x1b.xml","label":"October 4 · Bishop's at McGill"},{"url":"https://mcgillathletics.ca/sports/football/stats/2026-27/bishop-s/boxscore/12458","label":"Jerry Momo · player statistics"},{"url":"https://mcgillathletics.ca/sports/football/stats/2026-27/bishop-s/boxscore/12462","label":"Jerry Momo · player statistics"},{"url":"https://mcgillathletics.ca/sports/football/stats/2026-27/concordia-shaughnessy-cup-/boxscore/12460","label":"Jerry Momo · player statistics"},{"url":"https://mcgillathletics.ca/sports/football/stats/2026-27/laval-tva-/boxscore/12459","label":"Jerry Momo · player statistics"},{"url":"https://mcgillathletics.ca/sports/football/stats/2026-27/sherbrooke/boxscore/12461","label":"Jerry Momo · player statistics"}]},{"id":"2026-10-30-stfx-saint-marys","away":"stfx","home":"saint-marys","date":"2026-10-30","conference":"AUS","asOf":"2026-10-15","title":"X-Men, Huskies meet in AUS finale","paragraphs":["StFX has been finding the end zone. Saint Mary's has made a habit of keeping opponents out of it. Their late-season meeting brings the two strengths together.","The X-Men have won three straight, scoring 124 points against Mount Allison and Acadia. That run has taken StFX to 3–2 through five games, with an average of 30 points a game.","Saint Mary's is 5–0 over the same period and has allowed just 12.2 points a game. The Huskies beat Acadia 29–16 and 24–7 around a closer 24–17 win over Mount Allison.","Malcolm Bussey gives Saint Mary's a threat on the ground. He has rushed for 428 yards in the four games included in CanUFootball's totals and appears on the site's Hec Crighton Watch.","StFX has been good defensively too, allowing 15.8 points a game. That makes this more than a test of whether the X-Men can keep scoring. Saint Mary's also has to find enough offence against a defence that has been doing its share. Neither team can assume the room it found against other AUS opponents will be there again."],"notes":["Records and team scoring use regular-season results completed before October 15. Exhibitions are excluded.","Player totals use the available box scores and may be incomplete. The Hec Crighton Watch is CanUFootball’s own list."],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-30","label":"Official national schedule"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260905_olce.xml","label":"September 5 · Saint Mary's at StFX"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260912_s8sj.xml","label":"September 12 · Acadia at StFX"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_2r1j.xml","label":"September 19 · StFX at Mount Allison"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_6175.xml","label":"September 26 · StFX at Acadia"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261003_n4x7.xml","label":"October 3 · Mount Allison at StFX"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260911_aecb.xml","label":"September 11 · Mount Allison at Saint Mary's"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_vzdr.xml","label":"September 19 · Saint Mary's at Acadia"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_e8ye.xml","label":"September 26 · Saint Mary's at Mount Allison"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261002_b8gs.xml","label":"October 2 · Acadia at Saint Mary's"}]},{"id":"2026-10-31-bishops-concordia","away":"bishops","home":"concordia","date":"2026-10-31","conference":"RSEQ","asOf":"2026-10-15","title":"Gaiters seek more offence in Stingers rematch","paragraphs":["Bishop's and Concordia did not leave much work for the scoreboard in their first meeting. The rematch gives both offences a chance to improve on it.","The Stingers won 10–5 on September 26, their lone victory through five games. Bishop's is also 1–4 over that span, with both teams having struggled to keep pace with the higher-scoring RSEQ sides.","The Gaiters have averaged 14.8 points. Concordia has scored 11.0 a game, making the first meeting less of an exception than either offence would like.","Bishop's did produce 27 points against McGill in its most recent outing, but allowed 47. Concordia followed its win over the Gaiters with a 48–15 loss to Laval.","There is room for improvement on both sides of the ball, but the immediate need is finishing drives. One touchdown could carry considerably more weight here than it would in a game between the conference's higher-scoring teams. Bishop's needs more than five points; Concordia will want to avoid relying on ten being enough a second time."],"notes":["Records and team scoring use regular-season results completed before October 15. Exhibitions are excluded.","Player totals use the available box scores and may be incomplete. The Hec Crighton Watch is CanUFootball’s own list."],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-31","label":"Official national schedule"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260905_v7ru.xml","label":"September 5 · McGill at Bishop's"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-09-12","label":"September 12 · Sherbrooke at Bishop's"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260918_lxef.xml","label":"September 18 · Bishop's at Montréal"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_shbp.xml","label":"September 26 · Concordia at Bishop's"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261004_7x1b.xml","label":"October 4 · Bishop's at McGill"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-09-05","label":"September 5 · Concordia at Laval"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260912_ppda.xml","label":"September 12 · Montréal at Concordia"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_hi62.xml","label":"September 19 · McGill at Concordia"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261003_xhzw.xml","label":"October 3 · Laval at Concordia"}]},{"id":"2026-10-31-calgary-alberta","away":"calgary","home":"alberta","date":"2026-10-31","conference":"CW","asOf":"2026-10-15","title":"Dinos look to answer Golden Bears in return game","paragraphs":["Calgary put up 35 points against Alberta in September and still went home with a loss. The Dinos get another chance against their provincial rivals in the return game.","The Golden Bears won that first meeting 42–35, producing by far their better recent offensive effort. A week later, Alberta was held to three points in an 18–3 loss to Manitoba.","That inconsistency has left the Bears 1–4 through five games, averaging 15 points while allowing 40. Calgary is 2–3 over the same stretch and scoring 28.2 a game.","The Dinos also found a different way to play after losing to Alberta. They edged Regina 14–13 on October 3, getting a result without needing another high-scoring afternoon.","Alberta already knows it can move the ball and score against Calgary. The challenge is doing it again while getting enough stops to avoid having to reach 42. The Dinos need their defence to have a better answer than it did in September, or another productive offensive game could end with the same frustration."],"notes":["Records and team scoring use regular-season results completed before October 15. Exhibitions are excluded.","Player totals use the available box scores and may be incomplete. The Hec Crighton Watch is CanUFootball’s own list."],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-31","label":"Official national schedule"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260904_bx7n.xml","label":"September 4 · UBC at Calgary"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260911_j4p4.xml","label":"September 11 · Calgary at Saskatchewan"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_96n6.xml","label":"September 19 · Calgary at Manitoba"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260925_jbqx.xml","label":"September 25 · Alberta at Calgary"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261003_hww9.xml","label":"October 3 · Regina at Calgary"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260904_pg8n.xml","label":"September 4 · Regina at Alberta"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260911_19fu.xml","label":"September 11 · Alberta at UBC"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260918_mge2.xml","label":"September 18 · Saskatchewan at Alberta"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261002_k48e.xml","label":"October 2 · Manitoba at Alberta"}]},{"id":"2026-10-31-laval-montreal","away":"laval","home":"montreal","date":"2026-10-31","conference":"RSEQ","asOf":"2026-10-15","title":"Carabins get another shot at Rouge et Or","paragraphs":["Montréal scored 34 points against Laval in September. It needed more.","The Carabins get the return meeting at home after a 42–34 loss to the Rouge et Or, a game that showed how little either offence could afford to leave behind. Through five games, Laval is 5–0 and Montréal 4–1.","Their scoring averages are almost identical. Laval has put up 39 points a game and Montréal 38.8. The bigger difference has been on defence, with the Rouge et Or allowing 17.2 and the Carabins 22.2.","Laval followed the first meeting with a 48–15 win over Concordia. Montréal had a much closer afternoon against Sherbrooke, winning 23–17.","Victor Charland has thrown for 1,267 yards in the five games included in CanUFootball's totals. He and receiver Olivier Cool appear on the site's Hec Crighton Watch, giving Montréal familiar threats to prepare for.","The Carabins need more stops than they managed in the first meeting. They have shown they can score against Laval, but doing so again will mean less if the Rouge et Or are allowed to answer every time."],"notes":["Records and team scoring use regular-season results completed before October 15. Exhibitions are excluded.","Player totals use the available box scores and may be incomplete. The Hec Crighton Watch is CanUFootball’s own list."],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-31","label":"Official national schedule"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-09-05","label":"September 5 · Concordia at Laval"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260911_60uu.xml","label":"September 11 · Laval at McGill"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_yf7q.xml","label":"September 19 · Sherbrooke at Laval"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_3enl.xml","label":"September 26 · Montréal at Laval"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261003_xhzw.xml","label":"October 3 · Laval at Concordia"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-09-04","label":"September 4 · Montréal at Sherbrooke"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260912_ppda.xml","label":"September 12 · Montréal at Concordia"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260918_lxef.xml","label":"September 18 · Bishop's at Montréal"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-03","label":"October 3 · Sherbrooke at Montréal"},{"url":"https://mcgillathletics.ca/sports/football/stats/2026-27/laval-tva-/boxscore/12459","label":"Victor Charland · player statistics"},{"url":"https://rougeetor.ulaval.ca/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/boxscore-20260905-concordia-laval.pdf","label":"Victor Charland · player statistics"}]},{"id":"2026-10-31-mount-allison-acadia","away":"mount-allison","home":"acadia","date":"2026-10-31","conference":"AUS","asOf":"2026-10-15","title":"Mounties, Axemen renew matchup in Wolfville","paragraphs":["Mount Allison's first game against Acadia produced a 30–13 win. The Axemen will look to change that result when the teams meet again in Wolfville.","Neither offence has found scoring easy since then. Through five games, Mount Allison is averaging 15.4 points and Acadia 14.4, with both teams at 1–4.","The Mounties have lost their last three, falling twice to StFX around a 24–17 loss to Saint Mary's. That game against the Huskies was considerably closer than the 42–6 and 44–14 defeats against the X-Men.","Acadia has also faced a difficult run, losing twice to Saint Mary's with a 38–12 defeat against StFX between those games. The Axemen scored just seven points in their latest outing.","The first meeting showed Mount Allison can find enough offence against Acadia. The Axemen need to make that harder this time while keeping their own drives alive. In a matchup between teams that have spent much of the season searching for points, a few finished possessions could make a substantial difference."],"notes":["Records and team scoring use regular-season results completed before October 15. Exhibitions are excluded.","Player totals use the available box scores and may be incomplete. The Hec Crighton Watch is CanUFootball’s own list."],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-31","label":"Official national schedule"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260904_m54m.xml","label":"September 4 · Acadia at Mount Allison"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260911_aecb.xml","label":"September 11 · Mount Allison at Saint Mary's"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_2r1j.xml","label":"September 19 · StFX at Mount Allison"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_e8ye.xml","label":"September 26 · Saint Mary's at Mount Allison"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261003_n4x7.xml","label":"October 3 · Mount Allison at StFX"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260912_s8sj.xml","label":"September 12 · Acadia at StFX"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_vzdr.xml","label":"September 19 · Saint Mary's at Acadia"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_6175.xml","label":"September 26 · StFX at Acadia"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261002_b8gs.xml","label":"October 2 · Acadia at Saint Mary's"}]},{"id":"2026-10-31-regina-manitoba","away":"regina","home":"manitoba","date":"2026-10-31","conference":"CW","asOf":"2026-10-15","title":"Rams, Bisons prepare for another close contest","paragraphs":["Regina has been close enough to win several games without getting the result. Manitoba has already found a way through one of its own tight finishes.","The Rams lost to UBC by five, Saskatchewan by seven and Calgary by one in their last three outings. That left them 2–3 through five games despite allowing just 18.6 points a game.","Manitoba is 3–2 over the same span. The Bisons beat Calgary 38–36, then lost 31–6 to UBC before answering with an 18–3 win over Alberta. They have shown they can win with plenty of offence or with a defence that keeps the game under control.","Regina averages 25.2 points and Manitoba 22.0. Those figures do not leave either team much reason to expect a comfortable afternoon if the opposing defence plays well.","For the Rams, the task is finishing the job when a game stays within reach. For Manitoba, it is finding the balance it had against Alberta rather than leaving its offence trying to recover from a game like the loss to UBC. Both teams need their scoring chances to produce more than promising drives."],"notes":["Records and team scoring use regular-season results completed before October 15. Exhibitions are excluded.","Player totals use the available box scores and may be incomplete. The Hec Crighton Watch is CanUFootball’s own list."],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/composite?d=2026-10-31","label":"Official national schedule"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260904_pg8n.xml","label":"September 4 · Regina at Alberta"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260911_hvcf.xml","label":"September 11 · Manitoba at Regina"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260918_y81r.xml","label":"September 18 · Regina at UBC"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_u9sf.xml","label":"September 26 · Saskatchewan at Regina"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261003_hww9.xml","label":"October 3 · Regina at Calgary"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260905_gdvt.xml","label":"September 5 · Saskatchewan at Manitoba"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260919_96n6.xml","label":"September 19 · Calgary at Manitoba"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20260926_ncut.xml","label":"September 26 · UBC at Manitoba"},{"url":"https://en.usports.ca/sports/fball/2026-27/boxscores/20261002_k48e.xml","label":"October 2 · Manitoba at Alberta"}]}]};
